concept:australian-citizenship-legislation-amendment-act-2002-sch-2-sec-14c a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "14C Deferral of conferral of Australian citizenship"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-14c ;
    values:originalText "(1) If:  (a) a certificate of Australian citizenship has been granted to a person under this Division after the commencement of this section; and  (b) the person has not become an Australian citizen under section 15; and  (c) it appears to the Minister that:  (i) a visa held by the person may be cancelled under a provision of the Migration Act 1958 (whether or not the person has been given any notice to that effect); or  (ii) the person has been charged, or may be charged, with an offence under a law of the Commonwealth, a State or a Territory; the Minister may, in the Minister’s discretion, defer the conferral of Australian citizenship on the person until the end of a period determined by the Minister.  (2) The Minister must not defer the conferral of Australian citizenship on a person for a period that exceeds, or for periods that in total exceed, 12 months.  (3) If:  Schedule 2  Other amendments" ;
    skos:definition "(1) If:  (a) a certificate of Australian citizenship has been granted to a person under this Division after the commencement of this section; and  (b) the person has not become an Australian citizen under section 15; and  (c) it appears to the Minister that:  (i) a visa held by the person may be cancelled under a provision of the Migration Act 1958 (whether or not the person has been given any notice to that effect); or  (ii) the person has been charged, or may be charged, with an offence under a law of the Commonwealth, a State or a Territory; the Minister may, in the Minister’s discretion, defer the conferral of Australian citizenship on the person until the end of a period determined by the Minister.  (2) The Minister must not defer the conferral of Australian citizenship on a person for a period that exceeds, or for periods that in total exceed, 12 months.  (3) If:  Schedule 2  Other amendments"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "39599addbcdc735daba03e3d49c649172549f4a03ae2531fa161e500c8f132be" ;
    cof:pageNumber "13"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:australian-citizenship-legislation-amendment-act-2002-sch-2-sec-14c-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:australian-citizenship-legislation-amendment-act-2002-sch-2-sec-14c-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:australian-citizenship-legislation-amendment-act-2002-sch-2-sec-14c-ss-3 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <australian-citizenship-legislation-amendment-act-2002.pdf> ;
    dc:source "australian-citizenship-legislation-amendment-act-2002.pdf, p.13" .
doc:sch-2-sec-14c a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "14C Deferral of conferral of Australian citizenship" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "(1) If:  (a) a certificate of Australian citizenship has been granted to a person under this Division after the commencement of this section; and  (b) the person has not become an Australian citizen under section 15; and  (c) it appears to the Minister that:  (i) a visa held by the person may be cancelled under a provision of the Migration Act 1958 (whether or not the person has been given any notice to that effect); or  (ii) the person has been charged, or may be charged, with an offence under a law of the Commonwealth, a State or a Territory; the Minister may, in the Minister’s discretion, defer the conferral of Australian citizenship on the person until the end of a period determined by the Minister.  (2) The Minister must not defer the conferral of Australian citizenship on a person for a period that exceeds, or for periods that in total exceed, 12 months.  (3) If:  Schedule 2  Other amendments" ;
    cof:pageNumber "13"^^xsd:integer .

