doc:sch-2-sec-23ab-ss-1 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "23AB(1) Persons may resume citizenship lost under section 18" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(1) If:  (a) a person has ceased to be an Australian citizen because of section 18 (which deals with renunciation of citizenship); and  (b) the person has not attained the age of 25 years; and  (c) the person gives the Minister a written statement that complies with subsection (2); and  (d) the person gives the Minister, together with the statement, a declaration in the prescribed form that the person wishes to resume Australian citizenship; the Minister may, in the Minister’s discretion, if the Minister is satisfied:  (e) as to the truth of the matters contained in the statement; and  (f) in a case where the person has claimed that, if the person had not renounced his or her Australian citizenship, the person would have suffered hardship or detriment of an economic nature—that the person’s circumstances were such as to compel the person to renounce his or her Australian citizenship; and  (g) that the person is of good character; register the declaration in the prescribed manner and, on the registration of the declaration, the person making the declaration again becomes an Australian citizen." ;
    cof:pageNumber "15"^^xsd:integer .

concept:australian-citizenship-legislation-amendment-act-2002-sch-2-sec-23ab-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "23AB(2) Persons may resume citizenship lost under section 18"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-23ab-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) A statement made by a person under paragraph (1)(c) complies with this subsection if the statement is to the effect that:  (a) the person renounced his or her Australian citizenship in order to retain the nationality or citizenship of a foreign country; and  Schedule 2  Other amendments" ;
    skos:definition "(2) A statement made by a person under paragraph (1)(c) complies with this subsection if the statement is to the effect that:  (a) the person renounced his or her Australian citizenship in order to retain the nationality or citizenship of a foreign country; and  Schedule 2  Other amendments"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "9bfbc2571afe79d523d053da9fdae980c260687c065f0a66565e769fbee0d7c8" ;
    values:partOf concept:australian-citizenship-legislation-amendment-act-2002-sch-2-sec-23ab ;
    cof:pageNumber "15"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "A statement must comply with this subsection if it meets certain conditions." ;
